# The volume add-on's two Kubernetes sidecars (ADR 0083): the external-provisioner and the
# node-driver-registrar, built from source at the commits that the tags below are. The commit, not the
# tag, is the pin: the Dockerfile fetches that object and fails unless HEAD is it, and a tag can be
# moved. The driver, naru-volumes, is naru's own program (node/cmd/naru-volumes), built beside them.
#
# Why these releases (chosen 2026-11-21, from each repository's tags and GitHub releases): the
# external-provisioner v6.4.0, published 2026-10-09 (43 days before that date), and the
# node-driver-registrar v2.18.0, published 2026-09-04 (78 days before), are the newest stable releases
# at least two weeks old.
#
# Moved by: the PM, in a pull request that reruns `make image` and `make image-repro` and the QEMU test
# of volumes, when a patch release is at least two weeks old or an advisory is published for the
# pinned one. No bot proposes it.
PROVISIONER_REPO=https://github.com/kubernetes-csi/external-provisioner
PROVISIONER_VERSION=v6.4.0
PROVISIONER_COMMIT=72f13ee46fb93c11a72ef91549e70158283c03af
REGISTRAR_REPO=https://github.com/kubernetes-csi/node-driver-registrar
REGISTRAR_VERSION=v2.18.0
REGISTRAR_COMMIT=6f4e96f4222783370e4d2f3e3fc733b49c194a5f
# Licences (SPDX), read from the LICENSE of each source and checked by naru-release (ADR 0076).
PROVISIONER_LICENSE=Apache-2.0
REGISTRAR_LICENSE=Apache-2.0
